{{!
    @template mod_fastpix/view

    Renders the FastPix player wrapper. Phase D watch_tracker AMD module
    reads the data-* attributes on the wrapper element to bind itself to
    the player and route progress callbacks back to record_view_progress.

    Context variables:
      * playback_id              string
      * playback_token           string  (DRM JWT)
      * expires_at_ts            int     (unix seconds)
      * drm_required             bool
      * accent_color             string|null
      * default_show_captions    bool
      * activity_name            string
      * activity_id              int
      * cm_id                    int
      * asset_id                 int
      * session_token            string
      * no_skip_required         bool
      * initial_coverage_percent int     (Phase D — pre-computed % for first paint)
      * completion_watch_percent int     (Phase D — threshold from the activity)
      * current_position         float   (Phase D — resume position in seconds)
      * asset_duration_seconds   int     (Phase D — needed by tracker JS)
      * initial_intervals_json   string  (Phase D — raw JSON literal emitted via
                                          the triple-brace form lower down)
      * has_completed            bool    (Phase D — sticky once true)

    NOTE — do NOT write literal mustache examples (with curly-brace pairs) inside
    this comment block. Mustache treats the first close-pair-of-braces it finds
    in a comment as the terminator, so any embedded example would close this
    comment early and leak the remainder of the block as visible HTML.
}}
{{!
    The wrapper carries TWO sets of data-* attributes:
      - Phase C player-mount attrs (data-playback-id, data-playback-token,
        data-drm-required, data-accent-color, data-video-title) — read by the
        init script in view.php that creates the <fastpix-player> element AFTER
        hls.js loads. The element is NOT rendered inline because hls.min.js's
        UMD wrapper conflicts with RequireJS (CC9 silent failure); we have to
        defer mount until window.Hls is set.
      - Phase D watch_tracker attrs (data-cm-id, data-activity-id, etc.) —
        read by mod_fastpix/watch_tracker AMD module to bind progress callbacks.

    Player attribute names are pinned to the @fastpix/fp-player web component
    public surface (README + FastPix Web Player docs). `token` is the HLS-manifest
    JWT; `drm-token` is the Widevine/FairPlay license JWT. Per local_fastpix §3.5
    the same JWT serves both. Renaming without reading upstream docs is a CC9
    violation — the player silently renders an inert black box if attrs drift.

    Styling: rounded-3 + overflow-hidden + shadow-lg are added directly to the
    wrapper so the <fastpix-player> child gets clipped to rounded corners.
    The aspect-ratio:16/9 + black background stay inline (the JS contract does
    not depend on classes; the DOM mount uses querySelector on data-region).
}}
<div class="mod_fastpix-player-wrapper rounded-3 overflow-hidden shadow-lg"
     data-region="fastpix-player-wrapper"
     data-cm-id="{{cm_id}}"
     data-activity-id="{{activity_id}}"
     data-asset-id="{{asset_id}}"
     data-session-token="{{session_token}}"
     data-expires-at="{{expires_at_ts}}"
     data-no-skip-required="{{#no_skip_required}}1{{/no_skip_required}}{{^no_skip_required}}0{{/no_skip_required}}"
     data-playback-id="{{playback_id}}"
     data-playback-token="{{playback_token}}"
     data-drm-token="{{drm_token}}"
     data-drm-required="{{#drm_required}}1{{/drm_required}}{{^drm_required}}0{{/drm_required}}"
     data-accent-color="{{accent_color}}"
     data-video-title="{{activity_name}}"
     data-current-position="{{current_position}}"
     style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;background:#000;">
</div>

{{!
    Segmented coverage indicator with status pill. Coverage = unique seconds
    actually watched (drives completion + grade, only ever grows). The
    10-block bar paints one block per 10% of coverage; the active block
    fills proportionally. The pill on the right shows live status —
    "Processing" while below threshold (pink, pulsing dot) or "Complete"
    when coverage has crossed the activity's completion threshold (green,
    steady). Initial coverage % is server-pre-computed in
    playback_service::compute_initial_coverage_percent so the bar paints
    correctly on first frame. The tracker JS in view.php repaints it on
    every timeupdate.

    Per UX spec: position bar is gone; coverage is the only meaningful
    signal because it drives completion. Showing position confuses the
    progression message ("I'm at 80% — wait, why am I not complete?").
}}
<div class="mod_fastpix-covbar mt-3"
     data-region="fastpix-bars"
     data-threshold="{{completion_watch_percent}}"
     data-asset-duration="{{asset_duration_seconds}}">

    <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-card" data-region="fastpix-covbar-card">
        <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-track" data-region="fastpix-covbar-track">
            <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-watched" data-region="fastpix-covbar-watched" style="width:0%"></div>
            <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-needed"  data-region="fastpix-covbar-needed"  style="width:{{completion_watch_percent}}%"></div>
            <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-bonus"   data-region="fastpix-covbar-bonus"   style="width:0%"></div>
            <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-label"   data-region="fastpix-covbar-label">{{completion_watch_percent}}%</div>
        </div>

        <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-footer">
            <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-legend">
                <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-legend-item">
                    <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-swatch mod_fastpix-covbar-swatch-watched" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    {{#str}}coverage_legend_watched, mod_fastpix{{/str}}
                </span>
                <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-legend-item">
                    <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-swatch mod_fastpix-covbar-swatch-needed" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    {{#str}}coverage_legend_needed, mod_fastpix{{/str}}
                </span>
                <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-legend-item">
                    <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-swatch mod_fastpix-covbar-swatch-bonus" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    {{#str}}coverage_legend_bonus, mod_fastpix{{/str}}
                </span>
            </div>
            <div class="mod_fastpix-covbar-pill" data-region="fastpix-covbar-pill">
                <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="mod_fastpix-covbar-status" data-region="fastpix-covbar-status">{{#str}}status_processing, mod_fastpix{{/str}}</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

{{#js}}
require(['mod_fastpix/player'], function(Player) {
    if (Player && typeof Player.init === 'function') {
        Player.init({{cm_id}});
    }
});
{{/js}}
